1
00:00:11,760 --> 00:00:13,060
What's wrong, Yuumi?

2
00:00:14,640 --> 00:00:18,405
I have a feeling there's a lot
more at stake here than we think.

3
00:00:20,060 --> 00:00:22,280
This will require some explaining.

4
00:00:22,700 --> 00:00:25,780
While all VRMMOs originate
from the SEED program,

5
00:00:26,260 --> 00:00:28,697
there's a difference between
them and Elvime Online.

6
00:00:28,780 --> 00:00:30,100
You see,

7
00:00:30,600 --> 00:00:35,240
a stripped-down version of the Cardinal
System runs the other active VR Miss,

8
00:00:35,360 --> 00:00:38,097
but the one that operates
this game is a copy of

9
00:00:38,180 --> 00:00:40,977
the full-spec version
that ran Sword Art Online.

10
00:00:41,060 --> 00:00:42,440
Full-spec version?

11
00:00:42,780 --> 00:00:45,557
The original Cardinal System had a feature

12
00:00:45,640 --> 00:00:48,037
which could automatically generate quests.

13
00:00:48,120 --> 00:00:51,097
It would log onto the net
and search for various

14
00:00:51,180 --> 00:00:53,237
legends and folklore
from around the world.

15
00:00:53,320 --> 00:00:55,673
Then it would take the stories it found,

16
00:00:55,900 --> 00:00:59,900
adapt the data, and use it to
generate an infinite number of quests.

17
00:01:00,900 --> 00:01:02,540
How about this quest, then?

18
00:01:02,800 --> 00:01:04,980
Is it auto-generated by Cardinal 2?

19
00:01:05,700 --> 00:01:10,240
After seeing how that NPC was acting
just now, I have a feeling it is.

20
00:01:10,440 --> 00:01:13,558
If that is the case here,
then no matter what you do,

21
00:01:13,780 --> 00:01:16,545
this quest will end the
same way the myth does.

22
00:01:17,600 --> 00:01:20,177
Just now, I ran a quick
check on my archives.

23
00:01:20,260 --> 00:01:21,900
According to my data,

24
00:01:22,240 --> 00:01:25,740
in taking into account the
Norse mythology ALO is based on,

25
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:28,580
this quest must end in a final war event.

26
00:01:29,520 --> 00:01:32,317
The Frost Giants from
Jotunheim and Niflheim

27
00:01:32,400 --> 00:01:35,047
aren't the only ones
who want to attack Arun.

28
00:01:35,780 --> 00:01:40,427
Below Niflheim is a fiery realm called
Muspelheim, where the Flame Giants live.

29
00:01:40,720 --> 00:01:45,485
According to the myth, they will attack
the World Tree and burn it to the ground.

30
00:01:46,980 --> 00:01:49,060
Ragnarok, the twilight of the gods!

31
00:01:50,260 --> 00:01:51,090
Uh-uh.

32
00:01:51,173 --> 00:01:52,017
I don't buy it.

33
00:01:52,100 --> 00:01:55,217
I can't believe this game system
would destroy its own maps on purpose.

34
00:01:55,300 --> 00:01:56,771
It's got to be a mistake!

35
00:01:58,020 --> 00:02:00,549
I'm sorry, but there's
no mistake about it.

36
00:02:00,780 --> 00:02:04,797
The Cardinal System has the authority
to destroy its maps if it wants.

37
00:02:04,880 --> 00:02:10,240
I know this because the original Cardinal
System's last task was destroying Aincrad,

38
00:02:10,420 --> 00:02:12,773
the floating castle of Sword Art Online.

39
00:02:14,400 --> 00:02:15,320
No way.

40
00:02:17,520 --> 00:02:19,500
There goes my blacksmith shop.

41
00:02:21,120 --> 00:02:24,380
There go my chances of
ever meeting my soulmate.

42
00:02:24,860 --> 00:02:28,095
Even if this Ragnarok thing
happens and it all deletes,

43
00:02:28,620 --> 00:02:33,117
can't the server be rolled back the way
it was from one of the backups it's made?

44
00:02:33,200 --> 00:02:37,082
The system has an auto-backup
feature, but those files won't help.

45
00:02:37,300 --> 00:02:41,712
It only saves player data, not field
data, so you can't restore everything.

46
00:02:44,260 --> 00:02:45,480
Oh, I got it!

47
00:02:48,600 --> 00:02:49,797
I don't got it.

48
00:02:49,880 --> 00:02:51,177
You can say that again.

49
00:02:51,260 --> 00:02:52,440
Stop razzing me.

50
00:02:52,860 --> 00:02:56,095
I was trying to call a GM to
see if he knew about this.

51
00:02:56,420 --> 00:02:57,737
It ain't happening now.

52
00:02:57,820 --> 00:02:59,080
It's after hours.

53
00:02:59,340 --> 00:03:00,420
Support's closed.

54
00:03:01,120 --> 00:03:01,950
That figures.

55
00:03:02,140 --> 00:03:04,669
It's Sunday morning
just before New Year's.

56
00:03:05,900 --> 00:03:06,730
Kazuto?

57
00:03:06,813 --> 00:03:07,989
We're running out of time.

58
00:03:09,860 --> 00:03:10,690
Yeah.

59
00:03:10,773 --> 00:03:13,280
Let's hurry and get to
the last level. Right!

60
00:03:32,600 --> 00:03:35,400
Thank you.

61
00:05:07,800 --> 00:05:09,480
Damn it

62
00:05:19,220 --> 00:05:23,985
This isn't looking good, the gold one's
tough, nothing we do is slowing him down.

63
00:05:24,360 --> 00:05:25,800
Yeah, this sucks.

64
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:29,647
If we only had a mage who can
cast attack spells in our party.

65
00:05:30,360 --> 00:05:32,301
That's hilarious coming from you.

66
00:05:32,720 --> 00:05:34,817
It wouldn't help anyway
because the dude in the back

67
00:05:34,900 --> 00:05:37,857
with the high resistance to
magic would just move up.

68
00:05:37,940 --> 00:05:39,528
Could this get any tougher?

69
00:05:42,940 --> 00:05:46,840
Shockwave attack coming
up in three, two, one!

70
00:06:01,220 --> 00:06:04,120
Su-phila-heil-a-gul-austul!

71
00:06:05,080 --> 00:06:06,300
Flatsubal-a-bani!

72
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:13,830
Kirito!

73
00:06:14,200 --> 00:06:17,965
I've only got about two and a
half minutes before I'm out of MP!

74
00:06:18,460 --> 00:06:19,290
Kirito!

75
00:06:19,373 --> 00:06:22,660
Kazuto, more than two-thirds
of this medallion's gone dark.

76
00:06:22,940 --> 00:06:26,837
If we die now, we won't have time
to start over from the save point.

77
00:06:26,920 --> 00:06:28,420
Thanks! Good to know!

78
00:06:29,860 --> 00:06:30,820
Hey, guys!

79
00:06:31,080 --> 00:06:33,337
There's one thing we haven't tried yet!

80
00:06:33,420 --> 00:06:37,817
If we use sword skills with magic, we
might do some damage to this gold bastard!

81
00:06:37,900 --> 00:06:39,900
It'll leave you wide open, though.

82
00:06:41,720 --> 00:06:43,160
It's do or die time!

83
00:06:43,380 --> 00:06:46,537
So what do you say we focus
our attack and wipe him out?

84
00:06:46,620 --> 00:06:47,560
Hell yeah!

85
00:06:47,900 --> 00:06:50,194
Just say the word and his ass is grass.

86
00:06:57,200 --> 00:06:59,980
Silica, time for your bubble spell. Right!

87
00:07:01,740 --> 00:07:04,060
Ready, and hit it!

88
00:07:04,280 --> 00:07:05,960
Tina, bubble breath attack!

89
00:07:13,500 --> 00:07:14,900
Joe!

90
00:07:59,960 --> 00:08:00,790
Kirito!

91
00:08:01,940 --> 00:08:03,080
We locked up!

92
00:08:06,760 --> 00:08:07,740
This is it!

93
00:08:35,100 --> 00:08:36,980
Oh, my God!

94
00:08:45,220 --> 00:08:47,040
Oh, my God.

95
00:09:07,740 --> 00:09:12,280
This is how it comes to me.

96
00:09:25,040 --> 00:09:30,537
For this world, for this world,

97
00:09:30,620 --> 00:09:32,680
for this world, for this world,

98
00:09:57,260 --> 00:09:59,520
Ah, we killed your pal.

99
00:09:59,900 --> 00:10:02,040
Too bad for you.

100
00:10:18,180 --> 00:10:21,121
Okay, what the hell was
that move you just pulled?

101
00:10:21,340 --> 00:10:22,780
You don't want to know.

102
00:10:22,940 --> 00:10:23,820
Oh, come on.

103
00:10:24,100 --> 00:10:25,806
That was totally a new skill.

104
00:10:26,280 --> 00:10:28,045
Well, it's not really a skill.

105
00:10:28,380 --> 00:10:29,540
It's skill connect.

106
00:10:30,200 --> 00:10:31,320
Skill connect?

107
00:10:32,040 --> 00:10:33,511
Remember the last update?

108
00:10:33,940 --> 00:10:37,317
You know it brought a bunch
of sword skills to ALO, right?

109
00:10:37,400 --> 00:10:39,177
Well, even though we got those,

110
00:10:39,260 --> 00:10:43,201
we didn't get unique skills like
dual wielding or the divine blade.

111
00:10:43,540 --> 00:10:44,677
Well, hang on a sec.

112
00:10:44,760 --> 00:10:46,642
You were dual wielding just now.

113
00:10:46,900 --> 00:10:49,177
Technically, that wasn't dual wielding.

114
00:10:49,260 --> 00:10:50,090
Huh?

115
00:10:50,173 --> 00:10:54,497
I was using one-handed sword skills with
each hand and alternating between them.

116
00:10:54,580 --> 00:10:59,051
If I'm lucky, I can keep it going without
any lag maybe three or four times.

117
00:11:01,360 --> 00:11:04,917
Hmm no it's nothing
yui just deja vu is all

118
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:08,117
you're not off the hook
either what the hell!

119
00:11:08,200 --> 00:11:11,997
Did you do just now i
don't think you want to

120
00:11:12,080 --> 00:11:14,977
know oh come on i've
never seen anything like

121
00:11:15,060 --> 00:11:19,497
that before it's an
extra skill i picked up

122
00:11:19,580 --> 00:11:25,217
dual wielding don't pop

123
00:11:25,300 --> 00:11:26,997
a blood vessel all right.

124
00:11:27,080 --> 00:11:29,374
We can't stand around chatting all day.

125
00:11:29,820 --> 00:11:33,100
Leafa, how much time
we got left? Oh, right.

126
00:11:33,820 --> 00:11:37,577
At the pace we're going, we should
have maybe another hour or so.

127
00:11:37,660 --> 00:11:38,490
That's it?

128
00:11:39,180 --> 00:11:43,780
Yui, do you know how big these last
couple of floors are going to be? Yes.

129
00:11:44,300 --> 00:11:47,418
The third floor is about 70
% the size of the second.

130
00:11:47,580 --> 00:11:50,557
And the fourth floor is pretty
much just the boss room.

131
00:11:50,640 --> 00:11:53,977
I figure the last boss fight will
take us 30 minutes to finish.

132
00:11:54,060 --> 00:11:58,560
That means we only got about 30 minutes
to get to his room. That settles it.

133
00:11:59,040 --> 00:12:01,837
The clock's ticking and the
King of Giants is waiting.

134
00:12:01,920 --> 00:12:03,957
So let's get the lead out
and kick his giant ass!

135
00:12:04,040 --> 00:12:04,870
Daddy!

136
00:12:09,740 --> 00:12:10,570
You heard her.

137
00:12:10,900 --> 00:12:15,547
As soon as everyone's got their HP and
MP restored, we'll hit that third floor.

138
00:12:15,720 --> 00:12:16,550
Right!

139
00:12:31,140 --> 00:12:32,720
I don't want to go.

140
00:12:42,680 --> 00:12:45,920
Who are you?

141
00:12:47,480 --> 00:12:49,020
Who are you?

142
00:13:02,740 --> 00:13:03,660
Come on, guys!

143
00:13:03,800 --> 00:13:05,271
The last boss is waiting!

144
00:13:29,240 --> 00:13:30,757
Please, help me.

145
00:13:30,840 --> 00:13:32,300
Let me out of here.

146
00:13:36,060 --> 00:13:38,120
It's a trap. It's a trap.

147
00:13:38,280 --> 00:13:39,300
It's so a trap.

148
00:13:41,760 --> 00:13:43,557
Well, maybe it is.

149
00:13:43,640 --> 00:13:44,940
Maybe it isn't.

150
00:13:45,340 --> 00:13:46,693
What do you think, Yui?

151
00:13:46,960 --> 00:13:48,060
She's an NPC.

152
00:13:48,500 --> 00:13:53,265
Her core programming is connected to the
language engine module, just like Oortz.

153
00:13:53,500 --> 00:13:56,300
Although, there is one
difference between them.

154
00:13:56,620 --> 00:13:58,720
This one has an HP gauge.

155
00:13:59,100 --> 00:14:00,880
Yeah, that's a big red flag.

156
00:14:01,140 --> 00:14:03,997
If she's got an HP gauge,
we might have to fight her.

157
00:14:04,080 --> 00:14:04,910
A trap.

158
00:14:05,060 --> 00:14:05,980
Totally a trap.

159
00:14:06,340 --> 00:14:07,340
Obviously a trap.

160
00:14:07,880 --> 00:14:09,677
It might be a trap, it might not.

161
00:14:09,760 --> 00:14:10,590
I don't know.

162
00:14:10,800 --> 00:14:13,097
Either way, we can't
afford to take the chance.

163
00:14:13,180 --> 00:14:14,886
We can't waste any more time.

164
00:14:15,020 --> 00:14:18,880
We gotta get to Thrimmer
ASAP. Oh, right. Yeah.

165
00:14:19,300 --> 00:14:20,700
We got a job to do.

166
00:14:23,460 --> 00:14:25,740
Do not leave me. Please.

167
00:14:26,140 --> 00:14:27,180
I beg you.

168
00:14:33,620 --> 00:14:34,897
I know it's a trap.

169
00:14:34,980 --> 00:14:36,480
I'm not stupid.

170
00:14:37,560 --> 00:14:44,000
But even if it is a trap, even if
I know it's a trap, I don't care!

171
00:14:44,480 --> 00:14:47,657
I can't just turn my back on
someone if they need help!

172
00:14:47,740 --> 00:14:48,957
But even if...

173
00:14:49,040 --> 00:14:53,280
even if it means we fail the quest,
and even if Arun gets destroyed,

174
00:14:53,680 --> 00:14:56,677
if I got a chance to do some
good for someone, I will!

175
00:14:56,760 --> 00:14:59,642
Because that's what being
a samurai is all about!

176
00:15:01,440 --> 00:15:03,440
Don't worry, princess, I'm coming!

177
00:15:11,240 --> 00:15:12,070
I'm free.

178
00:15:12,400 --> 00:15:13,988
Thank you, fairy swordsman.

179
00:15:16,680 --> 00:15:17,800
No worries.

180
00:15:18,260 --> 00:15:19,540
Let me help you up.

181
00:15:23,160 --> 00:15:23,990
No.

182
00:15:24,280 --> 00:15:25,740
I can manage it.

183
00:15:28,460 --> 00:15:29,290
Whoa!

184
00:15:29,373 --> 00:15:31,420
The way out's kind of far, Dollface.

185
00:15:31,800 --> 00:15:34,212
You gonna be okay to make it on your own?

186
00:15:36,280 --> 00:15:40,420
I could, but I'm afraid I cannot
leave the castle just yet.

187
00:15:41,280 --> 00:15:46,162
For you see, I must first retrieve my
people's treasure, which King Thrimmer stole.

188
00:15:46,440 --> 00:15:51,028
If you would, fairy swordsman, please
let me accompany you to Thrimmer's room.

189
00:15:54,200 --> 00:15:57,520
This is beyond fishy,
don't you think? Uh-huh.

190
00:15:58,080 --> 00:16:00,080
Hey, uh, Kirito?

191
00:16:02,540 --> 00:16:05,440
Alright, I can't stand seeing you beg.

192
00:16:06,060 --> 00:16:09,017
Since we only got a little
further to go before the end,

193
00:16:09,100 --> 00:16:12,600
and seeing as how we don't
know for sure it's a trap...

194
00:16:15,200 --> 00:16:16,030
Yes!

195
00:16:16,113 --> 00:16:16,943
You hear that?

196
00:16:17,026 --> 00:16:18,777
You're coming with us, gorgeous!

197
00:16:18,860 --> 00:16:20,877
We'll help you beat that jerk, Thrimmer.

198
00:16:20,960 --> 00:16:23,737
We're in the same boat now,
so let's get wet together!

199
00:16:23,820 --> 00:16:26,040
Oh, thank you, fairy swordsman.

200
00:16:31,160 --> 00:16:34,660
Delete Klein's last comment
from your memory, Yui. Huh?

201
00:16:39,300 --> 00:16:40,130
Freya.

202
00:16:41,300 --> 00:16:43,120
Huh, she must be a mage.

203
00:16:43,300 --> 00:16:44,660
Her MP's really high.

204
00:16:49,760 --> 00:16:51,937
With the way they got
this dungeon laid out,

205
00:16:52,020 --> 00:16:54,844
the final boss room should
be down those stairs.

206
00:16:54,940 --> 00:16:58,937
Remember, he's the last boss, so he's going
to be way stronger than the other ones.

207
00:16:59,020 --> 00:17:01,373
When you hit him, hit fast and hit hard.

208
00:17:02,440 --> 00:17:04,537
Until we can figure out
his attack patterns,

209
00:17:04,620 --> 00:17:09,357
we'll be on the defensive so no one
moves on until I say one last thing!

210
00:17:09,440 --> 00:17:11,497
If you see his gauge
drop to yellow or red,

211
00:17:11,580 --> 00:17:14,617
his attack patterns are gonna
change big time so watch out!

212
00:17:14,700 --> 00:17:18,900
This is it guys get in there
and give it all you got!

213
00:17:34,620 --> 00:17:35,450
Let's go.

214
00:17:43,900 --> 00:17:47,760
Seiya, Fila, Zekken,
Hagel, Hogg, Margo, Ilto!

215
00:17:52,680 --> 00:17:57,180
Oath, Nazar, Fijo, Leged,
Jnada, Kalinda, Yochi!

216
00:18:02,020 --> 00:18:03,900
She boosted our maximum HP!

217
00:18:04,320 --> 00:18:06,438
I didn't know a spell could do that!

218
00:18:27,180 --> 00:18:28,560
Cha-cha-ching.

219
00:18:28,860 --> 00:18:30,566
I wonder how much Yul's here.

220
00:18:33,280 --> 00:18:35,500
Coo-chee-coo-chee-coo.

221
00:18:35,740 --> 00:18:37,480
Who let the flies in?

222
00:18:41,480 --> 00:18:44,520
The buzzing of their
wings is so irritating.

223
00:18:51,700 --> 00:18:58,620
I shall crush them all before
they annoy me any further.

224
00:19:27,640 --> 00:19:29,640
Winged alfheim insects,

225
00:19:29,980 --> 00:19:34,380
have you burrowed down here on
the whims of Urt, the trollop?

226
00:19:35,160 --> 00:19:37,560
Wretches, how dare you enter here?

227
00:19:37,800 --> 00:19:40,257
Did you think you could steal my treasure?

228
00:19:40,340 --> 00:19:44,928
If you tell me where I can find that
woman, I shall give it all to you gladly.

229
00:19:45,480 --> 00:19:48,317
Huh, you think a samurai
gives a damn about gold?

230
00:19:48,400 --> 00:19:50,917
Well, you can stick that
treasure right up your ass.

231
00:19:51,000 --> 00:19:53,059
Better yet, let me give you a hand.

232
00:20:01,420 --> 00:20:05,820
Lady Freya, how good of you to
grace us with your presence today.

233
00:20:06,220 --> 00:20:08,100
I see you have left your cage.

234
00:20:08,340 --> 00:20:12,693
Shall I take it you have come to your
senses and agreed to become my wife?

235
00:20:13,760 --> 00:20:15,407
She's supposed to marry you?

236
00:20:15,640 --> 00:20:16,980
Yes, she is.

237
00:20:17,520 --> 00:20:19,780
That is why she came to this castle.

238
00:20:20,100 --> 00:20:21,780
Isn't that right, my dear?

239
00:20:22,560 --> 00:20:23,390
However,

240
00:20:23,473 --> 00:20:24,937
the night before our wedding banquet,

241
00:20:25,020 --> 00:20:27,785
I caught her sniffing
around my treasure vault.

242
00:20:27,960 --> 00:20:31,560
As punishment, I locked
her in a cage of ice.

243
00:20:34,540 --> 00:20:37,180
Hey, Kazuto, I know this story.

244
00:20:37,380 --> 00:20:38,380
I read it before.

245
00:20:38,900 --> 00:20:44,860
Thrimmer and Freya, a stolen treasure,
and something else, too. But what?

246
00:20:45,080 --> 00:20:46,727
I will not become your wife!

247
00:20:47,120 --> 00:20:50,837
These warriors and I are here to
put an end to your reign of evil!

248
00:20:50,920 --> 00:20:53,155
I will return my treasure immediately!

249
00:20:53,780 --> 00:20:56,160
Yes, that's the spirit, my lovely.

250
00:20:56,580 --> 00:20:59,597
I would expect nothing
